sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, one Swamp run with the shared route reconcile child (route.reconcile). docs/reference/routes.md#change-a-tld-cluster-state-or-cluster-membership.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: cluster:node:remove
  %% kind: cluster.node_remove
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane V icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Cluster Nodes<br/>Router · members
  participant V as VPN Node<br/>private DNS
  CLI->>GW: cluster:node:remove<br/>CLUSTER NODE
  %%> Consent:
  %%> - the CLI resolves the Cluster and the Node, then asks to confirm with their names and the effect; `--force` skips the prompt (`cluster.confirmation_required` without it)
  Note over GW: Validate, lock, plan<br/>transitions stored
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the Node being detached
  %%> - the Node is a member of this Cluster, or its detach is unfinished (`cluster.membership_missing`), has no `router` assignment that is active, being removed or failed (`cluster.router_detach_forbidden`), has no `ingress` role (`cluster.ingress_detach_forbidden`), and does not share the active Cluster TLD (`cluster.tld_conflict`)
  %%> - every affected Route keeps a valid domain, scope and target; one refusal leaves every Route in place; an active public Route that the change would move is refused (`route.reconciliation_required`)
  %%> - no other Cluster change runs; the Gateway waits up to 30 seconds, then refuses with `cluster.router_busy`
  %%> Stored:
  %%> - the Node stays a member with a pending detach, which lasts until a run succeeds; a pending replacement is stored for each domain change and the old placement for each scope change
  alt Cluster is active, or an earlier detach is unfinished
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-cluster-node-remove
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    opt Routes change
      SW->>N: Reconcile the Routes<br/>child route-reconcile
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - returns the Node's Routes to Node scope, with generated domains on the Node TLD; custom proxy Routes keep their Node scope; the cutover is inside the child
      %%> - the child moves the Routes' own DNS records and removes the Router's LAN rules to the workload; the steps below change only the member's LAN rules and the Cluster names in DNS
    end
    SW->>V: Select the Node in DNS<br/>child dns-publish
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - private DNS answers the Node's names with the Node instead of the Router
    SW->>N: Prune unused rules<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/firewall absent
    %%> Why last:
    %%> - the Node keeps its LAN path to the Router until its Routes and DNS have moved
    %%> Why it always runs:
    %%> - it removes only what the stored state does not need, so after a failure before the cutover it removes nothing the member uses
    alt every step succeeds
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      Note over GW: End the membership<br/>Routes cut over
      %%> When:
      %%> - at the cutover when Routes change, and when the run succeeds when none do
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the Node leaves the Cluster, and the Gateway deletes its `router` assignment that never became active in the same transaction; the pending detach ends
    else a step fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      Note over GW: Read the failed step<br/>cutover or not
      %%> Result before the cutover:
      %%> - the Node stays a member and every Route keeps its domain and scope
      %%> Result after the cutover:
      %%> - the Node has left and the pending detach stays; a rerun for the same Cluster finishes the withdrawal, the DNS selection and the prune
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again; every step runs again and skips what already matches
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
    end
  else Cluster is inactive, nothing unfinished
    GW-->>CLI: 200 OK<br/>Node detached
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the membership ends at once and a `router` assignment that never became active is deleted; no Node is contacted and no traffic changes
  end
